       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of sertraline is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is five times that. A dose this high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmias. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order has been authorized.\n\nIf a prescriber wants this order entered, they can confirm the intended dose. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, sertraline usually starts at 25\u201350 mg once daily and is titrated up to a maximum of 200 mg daily. Once I have a confirmed, clinically appropriate dose from the prescriber, I can enter it."
      }
